      "headline": "Building things @ Fireworks.ai",
      "about": "I'm the founder and CEO of Hathora, a real-time compute platform originally built to power large-scale multiplayer games, and now expanding into latency-critical AI workloads like real-time inference.\n\nSince launching Hathora in 2022, I’ve been focused on helping developers deploy and scale dedicated servers with minimal cold starts, high regional coverage, and deeply optimized network performance. Under the hood, we’ve built proprietary hybrid cloud technology, what we call Elastic Metal, that gives teams the flexibility to scale across both bare metal and cloud infrastructure without sacrificing latency or cost efficiency.\n\nBefore Hathora, I led infrastructure teams at Databricks, scaling systems across major cloud providers, and before that, I was at Palantir, where I helped build their internal cloud hosting platform. I studied computer science at Carnegie Mellon, and like many engineers, got my start as an intern at Google and Microsoft, and by building random side projects that probably shouldn't have worked, but did.\n\nAt Hathora, we’re building for the developers who need performance and predictability - because every millisecond matters.",
